+# Volt subtle electric-car arches — 2026-10-31
+
+VSF01 follows the owner's rejection of the prominent fenders. Their outward projection falls from 55 to 12 mm in authored coordinates: **4.8 cm to 1.1 cm at world scale, a 78% reduction**. The transition into the flank is broader. A thin dark inner return replaces the thick painted rolled edge, giving the body a quieter, more integrated electric-car appearance.
+
+[Matched before/after views](evidence/volt-subtle-fenders-2026-10-31/before-after.html) compare the previous fenders with the new native Garage model. The [front quarter](evidence/volt-subtle-fenders-2026-10-31/final-gl/front-quarter.png), [front-wheel close-up](evidence/volt-subtle-fenders-2026-10-31/final-gl/left-front-low.png) and [rear arch](evidence/volt-subtle-fenders-2026-10-31/final-gl/rear-low.png) show the reduced rim.
+
+VSF02 retains the preceding front-wheel inset, complete opaque wheel housings, steering clearance, closed undertray and accepted low hood/cabin. The actual-buffer fixture passes 96/96 procedurally and prepared, including all 120/120 wheel-bay rays in each run. Its former 35–75 mm flare requirement is explicitly replaced by a 6–18 mm target for this owner correction; the other closure, clearance and silhouette checks remain. The exact task-start prominent-fender control fails the eight full/simple style checks and passes the other 88. The retained sports regression passes 104/104, including exact same-process parity across all 333 prepared meshes. Both desktop Compatibility and desktop Mobile produced nine final native views.
+
+Two runtime files change: `electric_reference_body.gd` and the prepared-root constant in `electric_reference_mesh.gd`. Resources use the separate `electric_subtle_fenders_v1` directory. Earlier fender resources are retained and hashed. Preparation also refreshes Electric's current modular assemblies, Garage template, shadow proxies and 52 preview pictures, so cached cars do not hide the revision.
+
+The initial mesh baker reused a cached assembly and produced only the night-light mesh. That incomplete result was detected before final assets were used. The reference baker now disables assembly caches, disables unnecessary batching, awaits model readiness and requires both authored hood variants. Existing modular preparation is restricted to Electric; concurrent other-car work is preserved.
+
+The actual App Garage/race check passes 58/58 with nine captures; its frame-hitch logs are retained and are not a performance result. The modular-assembly comparison passes 44/44 on recheck. Its first run recorded two reuse misses while the other 42 geometry/material/behavior checks passed; subsequent probes found matching keys, source hashes, eligibility and valid holders. Those initial results remain alongside the successful rerun. All 52 preview pictures were rebuilt and imported.
+
+[Actual results, commands, hashes and the task-only source checkpoint](evidence/volt-subtle-fenders-2026-10-31/report.json) record delivery. Every engine command uses the crash-dialog wrapper with an isolated offline profile. Windows certificate-store warnings remain in the logs. Reload/rebuild and owner appearance acceptance remain. No physical-device test/query, APK, live/backend/owner-save mutation, deployment, owner-process restart or main-index write was performed. Desktop Mobile rendering does not establish phone performance.
